  <section class="decisions-section">

    <div class="section-heading">
      <span>TECHNOLOGY DECISIONS</span>
    </div>

    <div class="decision-grid">

      <article class="decision-card">
        <span class="eyebrow">TECHNOLOGY DECISION</span>
        <h2>Why a Launch Template?</h2>
        <p>
          Individual EC2 instances are difficult to reproduce consistently.
          A Launch Template defines the expected instance configuration so
          new application capacity can be created consistently.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="decision-card">
        <span class="eyebrow">DESIGN DECISION</span>
        <h2>Why Multi-AZ?</h2>
        <p>
          Application capacity is distributed across two Availability Zones
          so that the platform does not depend on a single Availability Zone.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="decision-card">
        <h3>Cloudflare</h3>
        <p>
          Used as the edge ingress layer for authoritative DNS, edge SSL termination, proxying, and distributed denial-of-service (DDoS) mitigation.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="decision-card">
        <h3>Application Load Balancer</h3>
        <p>
          Provides Layer 7 HTTP/HTTPS traffic distribution across multi-AZ public subnets with continuous target health checking against the /health contract.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="decision-card">
        <h3>Auto Scaling Group</h3>
        <p>
          Ensures high availability and automated replacement of unhealthy compute instances across multiple availability zones.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="decision-card">
        <h3>RDS MariaDB</h3>
        <p>
          Isolates the persistent database tier in private subnets, completely disconnected from direct internet access, with automated backups and failover standby.
        </p>
      </article>

    </div>

  </section>


