    <article class="incident-card">

      <div class="incident-meta">
        <span>INCIDENT #001</span>
        <span>LOW</span>
        <span>ACCESS / COMPUTE</span>
      </div>

      <h2>EC2 SSH Authentication Failure</h2>

      <div class="incident-grid">

        <div>
          <h3>Symptom</h3>

          <pre><code>ssh ubuntu@&lt;public-ip&gt;

Permission denied (publickey)</code></pre>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h3>Investigation</h3>

          <ul>
            <li>EC2 was running</li>
            <li>Public IP was assigned</li>
            <li>Application subnet was correct</li>
            <li>TCP/22 was allowed from administrator IP</li>
            <li>Terraform showed <code>key_name = null</code></li>
          </ul>
        </div>

      </div>

      <div class="root-cause">

        <span>ROOT CAUSE</span>

        <p>
          The EC2 instance was provisioned without an
          EC2 key pair, preventing SSH authentication.
        </p>

      </div>

      <div class="remediation">

        <h3>Remediation</h3>

        <pre><code>key_name = var.key_name</code></pre>

        <p>
          The Terraform configuration was updated to
          explicitly associate the EC2 instance with the
          AWS key pair.
        </p>

      </div>

    </article>

    <article class="incident-card">

      <div class="incident-meta">
        <span>INCIDENT #002</span>
        <span>MEDIUM</span>
        <span>ROUTING / WEB TIER / APPLICATION</span>
      </div>

      <h2>Nginx Reverse Proxy 404 / Missing Upstream</h2>

      <div class="incident-grid">

        <div>
          <h3>Symptom</h3>

          <pre><code>$ curl -i http://54.236.188.6/health

HTTP/1.1 404 Not Found
Server: nginx/1.24.0 (Ubuntu)</code></pre>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h3>Investigation</h3>

          <ul>
            <li>Security group allowed TCP/80 ingress</li>
            <li>Nginx service was active (running) on EC2</li>
            <li>Nginx served static files from <code>/var/www/html</code> with <code>try_files $uri $uri/ =404</code></li>
            <li>Node.js app running on loopback: <code>curl http://localhost:3000/health -> 200 OK</code></li>
            <li>Inbound port 80 traffic was not forwarded to Node process on port 3000</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

      </div>

      <div class="root-cause">

        <span>ROOT CAUSE</span>

        <p>
          Nginx was installed with default distribution configuration serving static files from <code>/var/www/html</code>. No reverse proxy directive (<code>proxy_pass</code>) was configured to bridge incoming public requests on port 80 to the Node.js application process on port 3000.
        </p>

      </div>

      <div class="remediation">

        <h3>Remediation</h3>

        <pre><code>location / {
    proxy_pass http://127.0.0.1:3000;
    proxy_http_version 1.1;
    proxy_set_header Host $host;
    proxy_set_header X-Real-IP $remote_addr;
    proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-For $proxy_add_x_forwarded_for;
    proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-Proto $scheme;
}</code></pre>

        <p>
          Configured reverse proxy upstream in Nginx, validated syntax with <code>sudo nginx -t</code>, reloaded Nginx, and deployed the Node.js application as a persistent systemd service (<code>portfolio.service</code>). Validated <code>curl -i http://54.236.188.6/health -> 200 OK</code>.
        </p>

      </div>

    </article>

    <article class="incident-card">

      <div class="incident-meta">
        <span>INCIDENT #004</span>
        <span>COMPUTE</span>
        <span>RECOVERY</span>
      </div>

      <h2>EC2 Instance Failure</h2>

      <div class="incident-grid">

        <div>
          <h3>Scenario</h3>
          <p>
            An application instance was deliberately terminated to test
            Auto Scaling recovery.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h3>Expected behavior</h3>
          <p>
            The Auto Scaling Group detects the lost capacity and launches
            a replacement instance.
          </p>
        </div>

      </div>

      <div class="remediation">
        <h3>Validation</h3>

        <pre><code>Instance terminated
        ↓
ASG detected capacity loss
        ↓
Replacement launched
        ↓
Target registered
        ↓
Health check passed</code></pre>

        <p><em>Note: Unverified until controlled termination test is executed.</em></p>
      </div>

    </article>

  </section>


