    </div>

    <div class="failure-lab-grid">

      <div class="failure-lab-card">
        <span class="failure-lab-meta">SCENARIO 01</span>
        <h3>EC2 Instance Failure</h3>
        <p>
          Deliberately terminate an active compute instance in us-east-1a to validate target de-registration and automated recovery via Auto Scaling.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="failure-lab-card">
        <span class="failure-lab-meta">SCENARIO 02</span>
        <h3>Health Check Probe Failure</h3>
        <p>
          Introduce synthetic errors on /health contract to observe target state transitions from healthy to unhealthy and examine ALB routing behavior.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="failure-lab-card">
        <span class="failure-lab-meta">SCENARIO 03</span>
        <h3>ALB 502 Bad Gateway</h3>
        <p>
          Sever the proxy connection between Nginx port 80 and the underlying Node.js application process on port 3000 to trace edge-to-origin error boundaries.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="failure-lab-card">
        <span class="failure-lab-meta">SCENARIO 04</span>
        <h3>Database Connectivity Loss</h3>
        <p>
          Simulate security group rule desynchronization on TCP/3306 between application instances and private RDS subnets to test error handling.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="failure-lab-card">
        <span class="failure-lab-meta">SCENARIO 05</span>
        <h3>High CPU Resource Saturation</h3>
        <p>
          Inject synthetic CPU load on the application tier to verify CloudWatch metric alarms and trigger reactive scaling thresholds.
        </p>
      </div>

    </div>

  </section>


